CRITERION 3 — CurrentAge/SpouseAge carry is a strict improvement, no caller
depended on them being zeroed after Apply. PASS
  Callers of overrides.Apply (cmd: grep -rn "overrides.Apply\|RunWithOverrides"
  --include=*.go . | grep -v _test.go): settings.go:1185 (SettingsManager
  .ApplyOverrides) and mcpsvc/plan/overrides.go:19 Apply alias used by
  preparedWithOverrides -> RunWithOverrides. Both re-derive the ages before any
  read: prepare.From calls ComputeAges (prepare.go:56) and saveInternal calls
  ComputeAges (settings.go:769); ComputeAges (normalize.go:14-26) sets CurrentAge
  from the primary person and unconditionally does "s.SpouseAge = 0" before
  re-deriving. ValidatePersons (validate.go:26-66) is run on both paths and
  requires exactly one primary with a parseable BirthMonth not after StartDate,
  so the CurrentAge derivation cannot silently no-op and leave a carried value.
  Zero-sentinel grep (CurrentAge/SpouseAge == 0 / <= 0 / > 0) finds only readers
  of POST-prepare settings (analysis/ss.go:317,330; social_security.go:79;
  whatif.go:336) plus prepare_test.go assertions — none read Apply's raw output.
